course: dictionary
lesson: 9013
title: Skinned and the skin words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Skinned is the past of «to skin», which means to take the skin off something. You skin a tomato before you cook it, and a fox or rabbit is skinned in some places, like the animal's coat being taken away. «Skinned» can also mean you scraped some skin off, as in «I skinned my knee on the path.»
explain: Look at the words around skinned to find its meaning. If it is next to a knee, a bike or a plaster, it means scraped. If it is next to chicken, tomatoes or a cooking pot, it means the skin was taken off for cooking.
explain: The word skin can join with other words to describe a kind of skin. «Pale pigs can get sunburnt like fair-skinned people.» Fair-skinned describes skin that is light in colour. «The zebra is black-skinned with white stripes» describes skin that is black in colour.
explain: Skin can also describe a person's feelings. «You need to be thick-skinned to be a referee.» Thick-skinned means not easily upset when people criticise you. Thin-skinned is the opposite: it means easily upset. The skin here is not about your body at all.
fact: Skinned is the past of «to skin»: to take the skin off an animal or fruit.
fact: «If you have skinned your knee, you have scraped some skin off it.»
fact: The ending -skinned describes the kind of skin something has, as in «thick-skinned», «dark-skinned» and «smooth-skinned».
fact: «Thick-skinned» means not easily upset by criticism, and «thin-skinned» means easily upset.
fact: The phrase «keep your eyes skinned» means watch very carefully.
exercise: «After falling off his bike, Sam skinned his knee.» What does skinned mean here? | *Scraped some skin off | Bent | Broke his bike | Forgot his bag
exercise: «You need to be thick-skinned to be a referee.» What does thick-skinned mean? | Very hungry | *Not easily upset by criticism | Easily hurt by sharp words | Covered in thick fur
exercise: «Pale pigs can get sunburnt like fair-skinned people.» What does fair-skinned describe? | How fast someone runs | *The kind of skin someone has | How tall someone is | A type of hat
test: «Keep your eyes skinned for the bus.» What does keep your eyes skinned mean? | Shut the door tightly | Cry a lot | Close your eyes to sleep | *Watch very carefully
test: Which word means easily upset? | *thin-skinned | dark-skinned | smooth-skinned | thick-skinned
exam: «The zebra is black-skinned with white stripes.» What does black-skinned describe? | Where it lives | Its favourite food | How it runs | *The colour of its skin
